From: GLM-EXL3-2x-GB10 testing line <tensorfold-zig-testing@local>
Subject: glm-cuda: the latent attention FP8 key tiles load in 8-byte units, a tile ahead (Mia 1104 0005+0011, adapted to v1.2.3 + the paged marriage)

PROVENANCE: ported from MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-DGX-Sparks-1104,
patches/engine/0005 (latent attention reads FP8 key tiles in 8-byte
units ahead of their use) + 0011 (the latent attention chunks
256-thread launch is a named contract) (Apache-2.0, (c) MiaAI Lab)
against TensorFold v1.2.3 (6ec5fa4cb) + this line's adopted 6-patch
stack, 2026-11-07, by this line - a hand port (the fork's baseline
predates the paged-E4M3 marriage: our chunks_wide carries PAGED8 - the
page-table addressing for a sparse key's codes and scales - and the
port folds that addressing into the new fetch8 lambda; 0011's
contract naming lands as-is).

MECHANISM (0005): chunks_wide<HB, FP8> loaded a tile's E4M3 codes
byte by byte and converted them as it went, waiting for every load
before the tile's math. Each thread now fetches its 8-code units of
tile + 2 with one 8-byte read apiece (fetch8, __ldg on uint2) right
after the tile's first barrier, so the reads overlap this tile's
QK, softmax and PV, and converts them where load_kv(tile + 2) stood
(store8): the same cvt, row scale and bf16 rounding per value, so the
keys in shared memory are the same bits (little-endian code pairs
verified identical). The bf16 cp.async path is unchanged. Tiles 0 and
1 keep the inline fetch+convert through load_kv's FP8 early-return.

MECHANISM (0011): the 256-thread block both sides assumed by a literal
is now the named contract CHUNK_THREADS (a static_assert: a tile's
units split evenly; the kernel traps on any other width instead of
leaving keys unloaded); cuda_latent.chunk_threads launches it.

MEASURED (Mia, RTX PRO 6000 sm_120): decode dense chunks 58 -> 35 us,
sparse 72 -> 41-44 us; 0011: same SASS apart from the guard, HB32 FP8
167 registers (130 before the 8-byte loads), no spills, HB16 FP8 125.

PORT NOTES: glm_glue_attn.cuh - CHUNK_THREADS + static_assert + the
__trap guard; the fetch8/store8 lambdas (fetch8 carries our PAGED8
page arithmetic: dense keys at the bases moved once, sparse through
pt[src/CH]; uint2 loads are 8-byte safe - pstep is 16-aligned for
cp16); load_kv gains the FP8 early-return; the loop issues
fetch8(tile + 2) after the first barrier and store8(tile + 2) where
load_kv(tile + 2) stood. cuda_latent.zig - chunk_threads + the
launch. UPT: 8 units a thread (HB32 prompt), 4 (HB16 decode).
STAGING: applies on v1.2.3 + the 6-patch stack (verified byte-identical
to the port commit on a fresh checkout). OWNER: this line; STATUS:
EXPERIMENTAL, judged by the attnpref window (the content gate + the
decode rows, the definitive protocol).

